hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"642","Chapters on judgment in sales. 673 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The two sellers have the option as long as they have not parted, or their sale is with an option."
"643","674 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed me that Nafi' narrated to him, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two men trade, each of them has the option as long as they have not parted and were together, or one of them gives the other the option, and they trade on that, then the sale has become binding; and if they part after trading and neither of them has abandoned the sale, then the sale has become binding."
"644","675 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Jamil ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Wadi, he said: We went on one of our expeditions and camped at a station, and a companion of ours sold a horse to a man for a slave, and they remained the rest of their day and their night until morning. When the time of departure came, the man went to his horse to saddle it and regretted, so the (other) man held him to the sale, and they came to Abu Barzah, may Allah be pleased with him, and told him their story. He said: Do you accept that I judge between you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the option as long as they have not parted."
"645","676 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hammad - meaning Ibn Mas'adah - narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The seller and the buyer have the option as long as they have not parted, except in an option bargain, and it is not lawful for him to leave him fearing that he will rescind."
"646","677 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Qurrah narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever buys a musarrat has the option for three days, and if he returns it he returns with it a sa' of food, not samra'. Abu Amir said: meaning: not wheat."
"647","678 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever woman is married by two guardians belongs to the first, and whichever man sells a sale to two men, the sale belongs to the first."
"648","679 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If two agents sell, the sale belongs to the first, and if two guardians marry, the marriage belongs to the first."
"649","680 - Abu Zur'ah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from Umar ibn Qays al-Masir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, he said: Abdillah ibn Mas'ud sold al-Ash'ath ibn Qays captives from the captives of the leadership for twenty thousand, and he came to him with ten thousand, and he said: I sold you for twenty thousand. He said: I took them for ten thousand. He said: I accept in that your opinion. Ibn Mas'ud said: If you wish I shall narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I will do so. He said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If two traders trade a sale with no witnesses between them, the word is what the seller says, or they rescind the sale. Al-Ash'ath said: I have returned it to you."
"650","681 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Abu Umays, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: al-Ash'ath bought slaves from the slaves of the khumus (fifth) from Abdillah for twenty thousand, and Abdillah sent to him about their price, and he said: I took them for ten thousand. Abdillah said: Choose a man to be between me and you. Al-Ash'ath said: You are between me and myself. Abdillah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If the two sellers differ and there is no proof between them, then it is as the owner of the goods says, or they rescind."
"651","682 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Shafi'i, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: that a man bought a slave and used him, then a defect appeared in him, so he disputed about him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he judged that he return him. The seller said: O Messenger of Allah, he has taken his yield. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yield belongs with liability."
"652","683 - Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, he said: Makhlad ibn Khufaf narrated to me, from Urwah, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Yield belongs with liability."
"653","684 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sells pollinated palm trees, its fruit belongs to the one who sold it, unless the buyer stipulates."
"654","685 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the one who sold him, unless the buyer stipulates."
"655","686 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, that he informed him that he heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrating, that he heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrating, that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes bankrupt with the wealth of people, and a man finds his goods intact with him, he has more right to them than others."
"656","687 - Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Khabayiri narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Ayyash - narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whichever man sells goods and then finds his goods intact with a man who has gone bankrupt, and he has not received anything of its price - then it is his; but if he had received something of its price, then what remains, he shares with the creditors."
"657","688 - Ibn Awf narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Ayyash - narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same, and he added: And whichever man dies while another man's wealth is intact with him, whether he received something of it or not, he shares with the creditors."
"658","689 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning bankruptcy. 690 - Ibn Yahya said: Malik, Salih ibn Kaysan, and Yunus narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr, without attribution to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they are more entitled to the hadith, meaning: from the path of al-Zuhri."
"659","691 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Abi Fudayk informed them, he said: And Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Mu'tamir ibn Amr narrated to me, from Ibn Khaldah al-Zuraqi, who was the judge of Medina, he said: We came to Abu Hurayrah about a companion of ours who had gone bankrupt, and he said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged: Whichever man dies or goes bankrupt, the owner of the goods has more right to his goods if he finds them intact."
"660","692 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I sold a camel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I stipulated its riding back to my family."
"661","693 - al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Salim, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell me your camel. He said: I said: No, rather it is yours. He said: Sell it to me. I said: So-and-so owes me an ounce of gold, so it is yours for it. Then he took it and said: Ride it to your family. When I arrived, he ordered Bilal to pay me, and he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"662","694 - Hamzah ibn Malik ibn Hamzah al-Aslami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan - meaning Ibn Hamzah, his uncle - narrated to me, from Kathir - meaning Ibn Zayd - from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Muslims are bound by their conditions as long as they agree with the truth."
"663","695 - Hamzah ibn Malik ibn Hamzah al-Aslami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan - meaning Ibn Hamzah - narrated to me, from Kathir, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Settlement is permissible among Muslims."
"664","696 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, that Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki informed him, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you sell dates to your brother and they are struck by a calamity, it is not lawful for you to take anything from him; for what would you take your brother's wealth without right?"
"665","697 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Qays, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waived calamities (losses in crops)."
